IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa24-officers`
IMPORT `coa24-penalty`

-- coa24-register.l4: Part 35, ss 1092C to 1098 of the Companies Act 2006: privilege against self-incrimination, the
-- registrar's notice to resolve an inconsistency, removal of material from the register, rectification of the register,
-- and public notice of removal (lines 15485-15676 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively.
--
-- WHAT IS AND IS NOT ENCODED HERE. ss 1094(4)-(5), 1094A, 1097A(1)-(6), (8)-(10), 1097B(1), (3)-(8), (10)-(13) and
-- 1097C(1), (3)-(8), (10)-(13) are powers and duties of the Secretary of State to make regulations: machinery, inert
-- (reason 2) in NOTES.md. What those sections lay down for the court on an appeal, and the ceilings they set on the
-- offences the regulations may create, are encoded.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29; assumed, not ruled by a lawyer). MAYBE answers: JUST TRUE is the text
-- saying yes; JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words (each such branch carries
-- `-- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "<words>"`); NOTHING is "not covered" (each NOTHING branch says why,
-- as `-- NOTHING-kind (<why>)`). A function whose name ends "meets the requirement of s N" answers JUST FALSE when the
-- "must" it cites is not done: that is a fork line in NOTES.md, not a ruling.

§ `Part 35: correction and removal of material on the register (ss 1092C to 1098)`

-- ---- s 1092C ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1092C(2) offence` IS ONE OF
    `s 1092C(2)(a)(i) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A`
    `s 1092C(2)(a)(ii) an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911`
    `s 1092C(2)(a)(iii) an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995`
    `s 1092C(2)(a)(iv) an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979`
    `s 1092C(2)(a)(v) an offence under section 32 or 32A of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022`
    `s 1092C(2)(a)(vi) an offence under section 34 or 35 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907`
    `s 1092C(2)(b) any other offence, not within paragraph (a), an element of which is the delivery to the registrar of a document, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive`
    `s 1092C(2) any other offence`

-- src:15487 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than—
-- src:15488 | (a) an offence under one of the following provisions (which concern false statements etc)—
-- src:15489 | (i) section 1112 or 1112A;
-- src:15490 | (ii) section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911;
-- src:15491 | (iii) section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995;
-- src:15492 | (iv) Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979 (S.I. 1979/1714 (N.I. 19));
-- src:15493 | (v) section 32 or 32A of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022;
-- src:15494 | (vi) section 34 or 35 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907;
-- src:15495 | (b) any offence, not within paragraph (a), an element of which is the delivery to the registrar of a document, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive.
@ref s 1092C(2) The offences to which subsection (1) applies (src:15487-15495)
GIVEN offence IS A `s 1092C(2) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER offence
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(a)(i) an offence under section 1112 or 1112A` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— (a) an offence under one of the following provisions"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(a)(ii) an offence under section 5 of the Perjury Act 1911` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— (a) an offence under one of the following provisions"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(a)(iii) an offence under section 44(2) of the Criminal Law (Consolidation) (Scotland) Act 1995` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— (a) an offence under one of the following provisions"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(a)(iv) an offence under Article 10 of the Perjury (Northern Ireland) Order 1979` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— (a) an offence under one of the following provisions"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(a)(v) an offence under section 32 or 32A of the Economic Crime (Transparency and Enforcement) Act 2022` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— (a) an offence under one of the following provisions"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(a)(vi) an offence under section 34 or 35 of the Limited Partnerships Act 1907` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— (a) an offence under one of the following provisions"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2)(b) any other offence, not within paragraph (a), an element of which is the delivery to the registrar of a document, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) applies to any offence other than— ... (b) any offence, not within paragraph (a), an element of which is the delivery to the registrar of a document, or the making of a statement to the registrar, that is misleading, false or deceptive"
    WHEN `s 1092C(2) any other offence` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:15486 | (1) A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under section 1092A may not be used against the person in criminal proceedings in which the person is charged with an offence to which this subsection applies.
@ref s 1092C(1) A statement made in response to a requirement under section 1092A may not be used against the person (src:15486)
GIVEN `the statement was made by the person in response to a requirement under section 1092A` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `s 1092C(2) offence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1092C(1) the statement may not be used against the person in the criminal proceedings` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the statement was made by the person in response to a requirement under section 1092A`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A statement made by a person in response to a requirement under section 1092A"
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1092C(2) subsection (1) applies to the offence` offence
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (2) takes the offence out of subsection (1); it does not say the statement may then be used

-- ---- s 1093 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15498 | (1) Where it appears to the registrar that the information contained in a document delivered to the registrar in relation to a company is inconsistent with other information contained in records kept by the registrar under section 1080, the registrar may give notice to the company to which the document relates—
-- src:15499 | (a) stating in what respects the information contained in it appears to be inconsistent with other information in records kept by the registrar under section 1080, and
-- src:15500 | (b) requiring the company, within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the notice is issued, to take all such steps as are reasonably open to it to resolve the inconsistency by delivering replacement or additional documents or in any other way.
@ref s 1093(1) The registrar's notice to resolve an inconsistency (src:15498-15500)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar that the information in a document delivered in relation to the company is inconsistent with other information in records kept under section 1080` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1093(1) the registrar may give notice to the company` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the registrar that the information in a document delivered in relation to the company is inconsistent with other information in records kept under section 1080`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where it appears to the registrar that the information contained in a document delivered to the registrar in relation to a company is inconsistent with other information contained in records kept by the registrar under section 1080"

@ref s 1093(1)(a)-(b) What the notice states and requires (src:15499-15500)
GIVEN `the notice states in what respects the information appears to be inconsistent with other information in records kept under section 1080` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the company, within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the notice is issued, to take all reasonable steps to resolve the inconsistency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1093(1)(a)-(b) the notice is a notice of the kind subsection (1) describes` MEANS
    IF `the notice states in what respects the information appears to be inconsistent with other information in records kept under section 1080` AND `the notice requires the company, within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the notice is issued, to take all reasonable steps to resolve the inconsistency`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the registrar may give notice to the company to which the document relates— (a) stating in what respects the information contained in it appears to be inconsistent ... and (b) requiring the company, within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the notice is issued, to take all such steps as are reasonably open to it to resolve the inconsistency"

-- "the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the notice is issued": the day of issue is the first of the 14,
-- so the last day is 13 days after the day of issue.
@ref s 1093(1)(b) The period of 14 days beginning with the date of issue (src:15500)
GIVEN `date on which the notice is issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` MEANS `date on which the notice is issued` PLUS 13

-- src:15501 | (2) The notice must state the date on which it is issued.
@ref s 1093(2) The notice must state the date on which it is issued (src:15501)
GIVEN `the notice states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1093(2) the notice meets the requirement of s 1093(2)` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the date on which it is issued`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state the date on which it is issued"

-- src:15502 | (3) If the necessary documents are not delivered within the period specified, an offence is committed by—
-- src:15503 | (a) the company, and
-- src:15504 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 1093(3)(a) The company commits an offence if the necessary documents are not delivered within the period (src:15502-15504)
GIVEN `the registrar gave notice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the notice is issued` IS A DATE
      `date on which the necessary documents were delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registrar gave notice under subsection (1)`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the period specified" is the period of a notice under subsection (1)
    ELSE IF (NOT `the notice states the date on which it is issued`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the notice "must state the date on which it is issued" and the period cannot be counted without it
         ELSE CONSIDER `date on which the necessary documents were delivered`
              WHEN JUST delivered THEN
                  IF delivered AT MOST `s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` `date on which the notice is issued`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the necessary documents are not delivered within the period specified, an offence is committed" (they were delivered within it)
                  ELSE JUST TRUE
              WHEN NOTHING THEN
                  IF `date on which the question is asked` AT MOST `s 1093(1)(b) the last day of the period for resolving the inconsistency` `date on which the notice is issued`
                  THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the necessary documents are not delivered within the period specified" (the period has not yet ended, so no offence has yet been committed)
                  ELSE JUST TRUE

@ref s 1093(3)(b) Every officer of the company who is in default also commits the offence (src:15504)
GIVEN `the registrar gave notice under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date on which it is issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `date on which the notice is issued` IS A DATE
      `date on which the necessary documents were delivered` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `date on which the question is asked` IS A DATE
      position IS A `s 1121(2) position of the person`
      conduct IS A `s 1121(3) conduct of the officer`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1093(3)(b) the officer of the company commits an offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1093(3)(a) the company commits an offence` `the registrar gave notice under subsection (1)` `the notice states the date on which it is issued` `date on which the notice is issued` `date on which the necessary documents were delivered` `date on which the question is asked`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the necessary documents are not delivered within the period specified, an offence is committed by— ... (b) every officer of the company who is in default" (the condition is not met)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence of subsection (3) is not made out on the facts given
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `s 1121 the person is an officer in default` position conduct

-- The same duty as a regulative rule: the company must deliver the documents within the period (14 days beginning with the
-- day of issue, so the last timely day is day 13 when the day of issue is day 0). The trace clock counts days from the
-- day of issue.
DECLARE `s 1093(3) party` IS ONE OF
    `s 1093(3) the company`
    `s 1093(3) the registrar`

DECLARE `s 1093(3) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1093(3) deliver the necessary documents to the registrar`

@ref s 1093(3) The company must deliver the necessary documents within the period (src:15502-15504)
`s 1093(3) the company's duty to deliver the necessary documents` MEANS
    PARTY `s 1093(3) the company`
    MUST `s 1093(3) deliver the necessary documents to the registrar`
    WITHIN 13
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 1093(3) the company` BECAUSE "the necessary documents were not delivered within the period of 14 days beginning with the date on which the notice was issued"

-- s 1093(4): the text as rendered runs two versions of the daily default fine together ("...one-tenth of level 5 on the
-- standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale"). It does not say which version
-- applies, so both are encoded and a third value says the text does not choose (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
DECLARE `s 1093(4) version of the text` IS ONE OF
    `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of level 5`
    `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4`
    `s 1093(4) the text does not say which version applies`

-- src:15505 | (4) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (3) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1093(4) The punishment for the offence under subsection (3) (src:15505)
GIVEN version IS A `s 1093(4) version of the text`
      amounts IS A `s 1125 amounts the Act leaves to other instruments`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1093(4) the punishment for the offence under subsection (3)` MEANS
    CONSIDER version
    WHEN `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of level 5` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `s 1093(4) the text read as one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4` THEN JUST (Penalty WITH
        `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
        `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
        `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
        `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding an amount in pounds` OF (0.1 TIMES (IF 5000 AT LEAST amounts's `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds` THEN 5000 ELSE amounts's `s 1125 level 4 on the standard scale, in pounds`)))
        `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `s 1093(4) the text does not say which version applies` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text states two different daily default fines and does not say which one applies

-- ---- s 1094 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15507 | (1) The registrar may remove from the register anything that appears to the registrar to be—
-- src:15508 | (a) a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073 (power to accept documents not meeting requirements for proper delivery), or
-- src:15509 | (b) unnecessary material as defined by section 1074.
@ref s 1094(1) The registrar may remove material that appears to be a document accepted under s 1073 or unnecessary material (src:15507-15509)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar to be a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1074 it appears to the registrar to be unnecessary material as defined by section 1074` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` MEANS
    IF `it appears to the registrar to be a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1074 it appears to the registrar to be unnecessary material as defined by section 1074`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything that appears to the registrar to be— (a) a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073 ... or (b) unnecessary material as defined by section 1074"

-- src:15510 | (2) The power to remove material from the register under this section may be exercised—
-- src:15511 | (a) on the registrar’s own motion, or
-- src:15512 | (b) on an application made in accordance with regulations under section 1094A(2).
@ref s 1094(2) The power may be exercised on the registrar's own motion or on an application (src:15510-15512)
GIVEN `on the registrar's own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `on an application made in accordance with regulations under section 1094A(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1094(2) the power to remove material may be exercised` MEANS
    IF `on the registrar's own motion` OR `on an application made in accordance with regulations under section 1094A(2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The power to remove material from the register under this section may be exercised— (a) on the registrar’s own motion, or (b) on an application made in accordance with regulations under section 1094A(2)"

-- src:15513 | (3) The registrar may exercise the power to remove from the register anything the registration of which had legal consequences only if satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register.
@ref s 1094(3) Material whose registration had legal consequences: only if the interest in removal outweighs (src:15513)
GIVEN `the registration of the material had legal consequences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1094(3) the registrar may exercise the power to remove the material` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registration of the material had legal consequences`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything the registration of which had legal consequences"
    ELSE IF `the registrar is satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars removal unless the registrar is satisfied; it does not itself grant the power, which is in subsection (1)
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar may exercise the power to remove from the register anything the registration of which had legal consequences only if satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register"

-- Subsections (1) and (3) together.
-- src:15507 | (1) The registrar may remove from the register anything that appears to the registrar to be—
-- src:15508 | (a) a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073 (power to accept documents not meeting requirements for proper delivery), or
-- src:15509 | (b) unnecessary material as defined by section 1074.
