@ref s 1094(1), (3) The registrar may remove the material (src:15507-15509) (src:15513)
GIVEN `it appears to the registrar to be a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 1074 it appears to the registrar to be unnecessary material as defined by section 1074` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the registration of the material had legal consequences` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the registrar is satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1094(1) and (3) the registrar may remove the material from the register` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1094(3) the registrar may exercise the power to remove the material` `the registration of the material had legal consequences` `the registrar is satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "only if satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons"
    OTHERWISE `s 1094(1) the registrar may remove the material from the register` `it appears to the registrar to be a document, or material derived from a document, accepted under section 1073` `s 1074 it appears to the registrar to be unnecessary material as defined by section 1074`

