    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the registrar removes anything from the register otherwise than in pursuance of a court order, the court may, on an application by a person with sufficient interest, make such consequential orders as the court thinks fit"

-- ---- s 1096 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15538 | (1) The registrar shall remove from the register any material—
-- src:15539 | (a) that derives from anything that the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company, or
-- src:15540 | (b) that a court declares to be factually inaccurate, or to be derived from something that is factually inaccurate, or forged,
-- src:15541 | and that the court directs should be removed from the register.
@ref s 1096(1) The registrar shall remove material the court has directed be removed (src:15538-15541)
GIVEN `the material derives from anything that the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court declares the material to be factually inaccurate, or to be derived from something that is factually inaccurate, or forged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court directs that the material should be removed from the register` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1096(1) the registrar must remove the material from the register` MEANS
    IF (`the material derives from anything that the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company` OR `a court declares the material to be factually inaccurate, or to be derived from something that is factually inaccurate, or forged`) AND `the court directs that the material should be removed from the register`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any material— (a) that derives from anything that the court has declared ... or (b) that a court declares to be factually inaccurate ... and that the court directs should be removed from the register"

