`s 1096(3) the court may make an order for the removal of the material` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the registration of the material had legal consequences`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "anything the registration of which had legal consequences"
    ELSE IF `the court is satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- the sentence itself grants the power ("The court may make an order") on the one condition ("only if satisfied"), and the condition is met
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court may make an order for the removal from the register of anything the registration of which had legal consequences only if satisfied that the interest of the company, or (if different) the applicant, in removing the material outweighs any interest of other persons in the material continuing to appear on the register"

-- src:15544 | (4) Where in such a case the court does make an order for removal, it may make such consequential orders as appear just with respect to the legal effect (if any) to be accorded to the material by virtue of its having appeared on the register.
@ref s 1096(4) Consequential orders where the court does make an order for removal (src:15544)
GIVEN `the court does make an order for removal in such a case` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1096(4) the court may make consequential orders` MEANS
    IF `the court does make an order for removal in such a case`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in such a case the court does make an order for removal"

-- src:15545 | (5) A copy of the court's order must be sent to the registrar for registration.
@ref s 1096(5) A copy of the court's order must be sent to the registrar for registration (src:15545)
GIVEN `a copy of the court's order has been sent to the registrar for registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1096(5) the copy of the order meets the requirement of s 1096(5)` MEANS
    IF `a copy of the court's order has been sent to the registrar for registration`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A copy of the court's order must be sent to the registrar for registration"

-- src:15546 | (5A) This section does not apply to any material delivered to the registrar under Part 15.
-- src:15547 | (6) This section does not apply where the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter, for example under—
-- src:15548 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:15549 | (b) section 859M (rectification of register).
@ref s 1096(5A), (6) Where section 1096 does not apply (src:15546-15549)
GIVEN `the material was delivered to the registrar under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter (for example under section 859M)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1096(5A) and (6) section 1096 applies to the material` MEANS
    IF `the material was delivered to the registrar under Part 15`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to any material delivered to the registrar under Part 15"
    ELSE IF `the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter (for example under section 859M)`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply where the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsections say when the section does not apply and do not say when it does

-- Subsections (1), (5A) and (6) together.
-- src:15538 | (1) The registrar shall remove from the register any material—
-- src:15539 | (a) that derives from anything that the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company, or
-- src:15540 | (b) that a court declares to be factually inaccurate, or to be derived from something that is factually inaccurate, or forged,
-- src:15541 | and that the court directs should be removed from the register.
-- src:15546 | (5A) This section does not apply to any material delivered to the registrar under Part 15.
-- src:15547 | (6) This section does not apply where the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter, for example under—
-- src:15548 | (a) . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .
-- src:15549 | (b) section 859M (rectification of register).
@ref s 1096(1), (5A), (6) The registrar must remove the material (src:15538-15541) (src:15546-15549)
GIVEN `the material derives from anything that the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court declares the material to be factually inaccurate, or to be derived from something that is factually inaccurate, or forged` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court directs that the material should be removed from the register` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the material was delivered to the registrar under Part 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter (for example under section 859M)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1096 the registrar must remove the material from the register under a court order` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1096(5A) and (6) section 1096 applies to the material` `the material was delivered to the registrar under Part 15` `the court has other, specific, powers to deal with the matter (for example under section 859M)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not apply to any material delivered to the registrar under Part 15" and "This section does not apply where the court has other, specific, powers"
    OTHERWISE `s 1096(1) the registrar must remove the material from the register` `the material derives from anything that the court has declared to be invalid or ineffective, or to have been done without the authority of the company` `a court declares the material to be factually inaccurate, or to be derived from something that is factually inaccurate, or forged` `the court directs that the material should be removed from the register`

-- ---- s 1097 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 1097 direction` IS ONE OF
    `s 1097(2) that any note related to the material be removed from the register`
    `s 1097(3) that the court's order not be available for public inspection as part of the register`
    `s 1097(4)(a) that no note be made on the register as a result of the order`
    `s 1097(4)(b) that any such note be restricted to such matters as the court specifies`

-- src:15551 | (1) Where the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096 (rectification of the register), it may give directions under this section.
-- src:15552 | (2) It may direct that any note on the register that is related to the material that is the subject of the court's order shall be removed from the register.
-- src:15553 | (3) It may direct that its order shall not be available for public inspection as part of the register.
-- src:15554 | (4) It may direct—
-- src:15555 | (a) that no note shall be made on the register as a result of its order, or
-- src:15556 | (b) that any such note shall be restricted to such matters as may be specified by the court.
@ref s 1097(1)-(4) The directions the court may give on ordering removal (src:15551-15556)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 1097 direction`
      `the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097(1)-(4) the court may give the direction` MEANS
    IF `the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096`
    THEN CONSIDER direction
         WHEN `s 1097(2) that any note related to the material be removed from the register` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1097(3) that the court's order not be available for public inspection as part of the register` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1097(4)(a) that no note be made on the register as a result of the order` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 1097(4)(b) that any such note be restricted to such matters as the court specifies` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096 ... it may give directions under this section"

-- src:15557 | (5) The court shall not give any direction under this section unless it is satisfied—
-- src:15558 | (a) that—
-- src:15559 | (i) the presence on the register of the note or, as the case may be, of an unrestricted note, or
-- src:15560 | (ii) the availability for public inspection of the court's order,
-- src:15561 | may cause damage to the company, and
-- src:15562 | (b) that the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure.
@ref s 1097(5) The court shall not give any direction unless it is satisfied (src:15557-15562)
GIVEN `the presence on the register of the note or, as the case may be, of an unrestricted note may cause damage to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the availability for public inspection of the court's order may cause damage to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097(5) the court may give a direction` MEANS
    IF (`the presence on the register of the note or, as the case may be, of an unrestricted note may cause damage to the company` OR `the availability for public inspection of the court's order may cause damage to the company`) AND `the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection bars a direction unless the court is satisfied of both limbs; it does not itself grant the power, which is in subsections (1) to (4)
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall not give any direction under this section unless it is satisfied— (a) that— ... may cause damage to the company, and (b) that the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure"

-- Subsections (1) to (5) together: the court may give the direction if it has made the order and, where it is not satisfied of
-- the matters in (5), not otherwise.
-- src:15551 | (1) Where the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096 (rectification of the register), it may give directions under this section.
-- src:15552 | (2) It may direct that any note on the register that is related to the material that is the subject of the court's order shall be removed from the register.
-- src:15553 | (3) It may direct that its order shall not be available for public inspection as part of the register.
-- src:15554 | (4) It may direct—
-- src:15555 | (a) that no note shall be made on the register as a result of its order, or
-- src:15556 | (b) that any such note shall be restricted to such matters as may be specified by the court.
-- src:15557 | (5) The court shall not give any direction under this section unless it is satisfied—
-- src:15558 | (a) that—
-- src:15559 | (i) the presence on the register of the note or, as the case may be, of an unrestricted note, or
-- src:15560 | (ii) the availability for public inspection of the court's order,
-- src:15561 | may cause damage to the company, and
-- src:15562 | (b) that the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure.
@ref s 1097(1)-(5) The court may give the direction (src:15551-15556) (src:15557-15562)
GIVEN direction IS A `s 1097 direction`
      `the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the presence on the register of the note or, as the case may be, of an unrestricted note may cause damage to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the availability for public inspection of the court's order may cause damage to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097(1)-(5) the court may give the direction on these facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1097(1)-(4) the court may give the direction` direction `the court makes an order for the removal of anything from the register under section 1096`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        CONSIDER `s 1097(5) the court may give a direction` `the presence on the register of the note or, as the case may be, of an unrestricted note may cause damage to the company` `the availability for public inspection of the court's order may cause damage to the company` `the company's interest in non-disclosure outweighs any interest of other persons in disclosure`
        WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall not give any direction under this section unless it is satisfied"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the court has not made an order for removal under section 1096

-- ---- ss 1097A, 1097B, 1097C: what the Act itself lays down for the regulations ----------------------------

-- s 1097A(5)(a): the regulations may suspend certain duties "for up to 28 days beginning with the date on which it is
-- registered": so the last day of a full suspension is 27 days after the day of registration.
-- src:15588 | (5) Provision made by virtue of subsection (3)(i) may in particular include provision, in relation to the registration of a default address—
-- src:15589 | (a) for the suspension, for up to 28 days beginning with the date on which it is registered, of duties of the company under this Act relating to the inspection of company records or to the provision, disclosure or display of information,
@ref s 1097A(5)(a) A suspension of up to 28 days beginning with the date of registration (src:15588-15589)
GIVEN `days of suspension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097A(5)(a) the regulations may provide for a suspension of this length` MEANS
    IF `days of suspension` AT MOST 28
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for the suspension, for up to 28 days beginning with the date on which it is registered"

@ref s 1097A(5)(a) The last day of a suspension of 28 days beginning with the date of registration (src:15589)
GIVEN `date on which the default address is registered` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1097A(5)(a) the last day of a suspension of 28 days` MEANS `date on which the default address is registered` PLUS 27

-- s 1097A(4A)(a), s 1097B(6), s 1097C(6): "summary offences punishable with a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale
-- and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale".
-- src:15582 | (a) provision creating summary offences punishable with a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale;
@ref s 1097A(4A)(a) The offences the regulations may create (src:15582)
`s 1097A(4A)(a) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:15627 | (6) The provision made by virtue of subsection (5)(k) may in particular include provision creating summary offences punishable with a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1097B(6) The offences the regulations may create (src:15627)
`s 1097B(6) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- src:15661 | (6) The provision made by virtue of subsection (5)(k) may in particular include provision creating summary offences punishable with a fine not exceeding level 3 on the standard scale and, for continued contravention, a daily default fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 3 on the standard scale.
@ref s 1097C(6) The offences the regulations may create (src:15661)
`s 1097C(6) the punishment for a summary offence in the regulations` MEANS Penalty WITH
    `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
    `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
    `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 1)
    `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 3, 0.1)
    `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

-- On an appeal under the regulations, the court must direct the registrar to register such address as the court
