    IF `an appeal has been brought to the court under the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an appeal"

-- src:15664 | (9) On an appeal, the court must direct the registrar to register such address as the principal office of the relevant person as the court considers appropriate in all the circumstances of the case.
@ref s 1097C(9) On an appeal the court must direct the registrar to register an appropriate principal office address (src:15664)
GIVEN `an appeal has been brought to the court under the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
