`s 1097C(9) the court must direct the registrar to register such address as the principal office of the relevant person as the court considers appropriate` MEANS
    IF `an appeal has been brought to the court under the regulations`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On an appeal"

-- s 1097A(3)(h), s 1097B(5)(j), s 1097C(5)(j): "default address" is an address the registrar nominates; the label itself
-- is defined by those paragraphs and carries no rule of its own (the nomination is a power the regulations may confer).

-- s 1097B(2) and s 1097C(2): the defined terms. The seam to s 790C (registrable person, registrable relevant legal entity)
-- is an input that answers MAYBE BOOLEAN.
-- src:15607 | “registered service address”, in relation to a relevant person, means the address for the time being shown in the register as the person’s current service address;
@ref s 1097B(2) "registered service address" (src:15607)
GIVEN `the address is the address for the time being shown in the register as the person's current service address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097B(2) the address is the registered service address of the relevant person` MEANS
    IF `the address is the address for the time being shown in the register as the person's current service address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“registered service address”, in relation to a relevant person, means the address for the time being shown in the register as the person’s current service address"

-- src:15608 | “relevant person” means—
-- src:15609 | (a) a director of a company that is not an overseas company,
-- src:15610 | (b) a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company, or
-- src:15611 | (c) a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company (within the meanings given by section 790C).
@ref s 1097B(2) "relevant person" (src:15608-15611)
GIVEN `the person is a director of a company that is not an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 790C the person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097B(2) the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of a company that is not an overseas company` OR `the person is a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 790C the person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant person” means— (a) a director of a company that is not an overseas company, (b) a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company, or (c) a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity"
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a registrable person or registrable relevant legal entity is defined by section 790C, which is not in this part

-- src:15640 | “address registered as the principal office”, in relation to a relevant person, means the address for the time being shown in the register as the address of the person’s current principal office;
@ref s 1097C(2) "address registered as the principal office" (src:15640)
GIVEN `the address is the address for the time being shown in the register as the address of the person's current principal office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097C(2) the address is the address registered as the principal office of the relevant person` MEANS
    IF `the address is the address for the time being shown in the register as the address of the person's current principal office`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“address registered as the principal office”, in relation to a relevant person, means the address for the time being shown in the register as the address of the person’s current principal office"

-- src:15641 | “relevant person” means—
-- src:15642 | (a) a director of a company that is not an overseas company,
-- src:15643 | (b) a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company,
-- src:15644 | (c) a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company (within the meaning given by section 790C), or
-- src:15645 | (d) a registrable person in relation to a company (within the meaning given by section 790C) who falls within section 790C(12).
@ref s 1097C(2) "relevant person" (src:15641-15645)
GIVEN `the person is a director of a company that is not an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 790C the person is a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 790C(12) the person is a registrable person in relation to a company who falls within section 790C(12)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1097C(2) the person is a relevant person` MEANS
    IF `the person is a director of a company that is not an overseas company` OR `the person is a secretary or one of the joint secretaries of a company that is not an overseas company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 790C the person is a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN
             CONSIDER `s 790C(12) the person is a registrable person in relation to a company who falls within section 790C(12)`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant person” means— (a) a director ..., (b) a secretary ..., (c) a registrable relevant legal entity in relation to a company ..., or (d) a registrable person in relation to a company ... who falls within section 790C(12)"
             WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person falls within section 790C(12) is defined by section 790C, which is not in this part
         WHEN NOTHING THEN
             CONSIDER `s 790C(12) the person is a registrable person in relation to a company who falls within section 790C(12)`
             WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is a registrable relevant legal entity is defined by section 790C, which is not in this part

-- ---- s 1098 ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:15672 | (1) The registrar must cause to be published—
-- src:15673 | (a) in the Gazette, or
-- src:15674 | (b) in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice),
-- src:15675 | notice of the removal from the register of an enhanced disclosure document (see section 1078) or of any material derived from such a document.
@ref s 1098(1) The registrar must publish notice of the removal of an enhanced disclosure document (src:15672-15675)
GIVEN `s 1078 the material removed is an enhanced disclosure document, or material derived from such a document` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098(1) the registrar must cause notice of the removal to be published` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 1078 the material removed is an enhanced disclosure document, or material derived from such a document`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "notice of the removal from the register of an enhanced disclosure document (see section 1078) or of any material derived from such a document"

@ref s 1098(1)(a), (b) The notice is published in the Gazette or in accordance with section 1116 (src:15673-15674)
GIVEN `the notice has been published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice has been published in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098(1) the publication meets the requirement of s 1098(1)` MEANS
    IF `the notice has been published in the Gazette` OR `the notice has been published in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The registrar must cause to be published— (a) in the Gazette, or (b) in accordance with section 1116 (alternative means of giving public notice), notice of the removal"

-- src:15676 | (2) The notice must state the name and registered number of the company, the description of document and the date of receipt.
@ref s 1098(2) What the notice must state (src:15676)
GIVEN `the notice states the name of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the registered number of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the description of document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice states the date of receipt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1098(2) the notice meets the requirement of s 1098(2)` MEANS
    IF `the notice states the name of the company` AND `the notice states the registered number of the company` AND `the notice states the description of document` AND `the notice states the date of receipt`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The notice must state the name and registered number of the company, the description of document and the date of receipt"
